where $\beta_k$ is the variance at each step of a fixed schedule, and with a large enough $K$ we get $q(\boldsymbol{\tau}^K) \approx \mathcal{N}(\boldsymbol{\tau}^K; \mathbf{0}, \mathbf{I})$.
