In this work, we consider centralized strategies for both teams. 
Namely, a coordinator decides the next allocation for its own team and sends instructions to the robots within its team to follow.
Consequently, the only intelligent agents are the defender{} coordinator and the attacker{} coordinator, which we refer to as the defender{} and the attacker{} for simplicity.
Our formulation also leads to feedback strategies that re-allocate resources based on the system state (the current allocation of the attacker{} team and the defender{} team). 
The re-allocation is done with all possible next actions of the opposing team in mind. 
