\section{Background}\label{}
In this paper we present a PLP framework, \smp{} based on ProbLog2: we describe the relevant background about syntax, the semantics for the probabilistic component of ProbLog programs and the semantics for the models of a logic program we will consider throughout the paper. We also describe the corresponding inference and learning tasks under the new semantics. Finally, we also consider the application of \smp{} to probabilistic argumentation problems, hence we discuss the required background in argumentation.

